{%- comment -%} ============ FAQ ============ {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="pd-page faq" id="faq-list-{{ section.id }}" aria-labelledby="faq-title-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="pd-wrap faq__grid">
    <div class="faq__head">
      <h2 id="faq-title-{{ section.id }}" style="color: #0a0c10 !important;">Questions?<br>We've got sticks.</h2>
      <p>Everything you need to know before your first throw.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq__list">
      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>What surfaces does Popdarts work on?</summary>
        <p>Any smooth, flat surface — driveways, patios, hardwood, tile, even carpet with the Swaptop board. Indoors or out, it sets up in under a minute.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>What age is Popdarts good for?</summary>
        <p>5 to 95. The Rookie Pack uses softer darts built for younger throwers; the Pro Pack is tournament-weight for older kids and adults. Most families end up owning both.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>How is a round scored?</summary>
        <p>Closest dart to the Target Marker scores 3, every other stuck dart adds 1, and a dart landing directly on the marker is an instant 10. Cancellation scoring settles the round, and first team to 21 wins the match.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>What's included in the Pro Pack?</summary>
        <p>6 Pro Popdarts (2 sets of 3), 1 Pro Target Marker, game rules, a carrying bag with a built-in ruler, and 4 stickers — everything you need for your first match.</p>
